# Ola CRM backend — per-machine secrets.
# Copy this file to `backend/.env` and fill in the real values before running
# `bash start-dev.sh`. See `ola/SETUP.md` for where each value comes from.
#
# This file is the SINGLE source of local-dev config. start-dev.sh sources ONLY
# backend/.env — the prod bundle .secrets/SERVERS.env is deploy-only and is never
# read for local dev. Anything start-dev.sh needs must live here.
#
# Never commit backend/.env — it is gitignored.

# ------------------ Required ------------------

# MongoDB — the dedicated local-dev Atlas cluster (host `ola-local.dmbtqkq`).
# start-dev.sh whitelists this host and REFUSES to start against staging
# (ola-dev) or prod (cluster0). Ask zyd for the URI; the db name is free.
DATABASE="mongodb+srv://ola-local-user:password@ola-local.dmbtqkq.mongodb.net/olalocal?retryWrites=true&w=majority&appName=ola-local"

# Any strong random string. Generate once: `openssl rand -hex 32`
JWT_SECRET="your_private_jwt_secret_key"

# NanoBot ↔ MCP server loopback service token (used only between two local
# processes on 127.0.0.1). Dev machines can share the same value; prod
# generates a fresh one. Generate: `openssl rand -hex 32`
MCP_SERVICE_TOKEN="your_mcp_service_token_hex"

# NanoBot's default LLM provider (model `deepseek-v4-flash`) — powers Ask Ola.
# Get from https://platform.deepseek.com → API keys.
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY="sk-..."

# ------------------ NanoBot channels (required by start-dev.sh) ------------------
# start-dev.sh renders ~/.nanobot/config.json from these on every boot and
# refuses to start if any is missing. They previously came from the prod bundle
# .secrets/SERVERS.env, which is no longer sourced locally — paste the dev-shared
# values here (ask zyd). Whether email actually polls is a separate concern; these
# four are needed only so the config renders.
ZOHO_OLA_EMAIL="your_zoho_account@olatech.ai"
ZOHO_OLA_APP_PASSWORD="your_zoho_app_password"
ZOHO_IMAP_HOST="imap.zoho.com"
ZOHO_SMTP_HOST="smtp.zoho.com"

# Alternate LLM provider (gemini). Optional — only if you switch a nanobot agent
# off deepseek. Get from https://aistudio.google.com.
# GEMINI_API_KEY="AIza..."

# ------------------ Audio transcription (sales-coach) ------------------

# Provider dispatch (#257) — runtime engine selection:
#   admin.transcribeProvider > TRANSCRIPTION_PROVIDER env > hardcoded 'openai'
# Per-admin override beats this env var, so leave unset unless you want a
# process-wide default. Valid values: openai | paraformer.
# TRANSCRIPTION_PROVIDER="openai"

# --- OpenAI gpt-4o-transcribe-diarize (push, multipart) ---
# Required when any admin/job will be routed to OpenAI.
# Get from https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# OPENAI_API_KEY="sk-..."

# --- DashScope Paraformer-v2 (pull, async REST) ---
# Required when any admin is routed to paraformer. HK Cantonese first-class,
# 9× cheaper than OpenAI on long-form. Sign up at https://bailian.console.aliyun.com
# DASHSCOPE_API_KEY="sk-..."

# Public URL that DashScope can fetch the audio file from. Local dev: set by
# start-dev-paraformer.sh automatically (cloudflared trycloudflare). Prod
# Box1: direct public IP to bypass Cloudflare WAF (which blocks Aliyun IPs).
# Required when paraformer is the active provider for any upload.
#   Local : (auto-injected by start-dev-paraformer.sh — DO NOT set manually)
#   Prod  : BACKEND_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://47.77.239.237
# BACKEND_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=""

# Optional paraformer tunables (defaults are good for HK 2-speaker sales calls).
# PARAFORMER_LANG_HINTS="yue,zh,en"        # Cantonese first, Mandarin + English fallback
# PARAFORMER_SPEAKER_COUNT="2"             # sales + customer
# PARAFORMER_POLL_INTERVAL_MS="5000"       # poll cadence + heartbeat refresh
# PARAFORMER_MAX_WAIT_MS="1800000"         # 30 min hard timeout per job

# ------------------ Common ------------------

NODE_ENV="development"
OPENSSL_CONF="/dev/null"
PUBLIC_SERVER_FILE="http://localhost:8888/"

# #266 — environment gate. Local dev leaves this unset (or =dev). Production
# Box1's backend/.env MUST set OLA_ENV=prod so start-dev.sh refuses to run
# there (which would otherwise point local processes at the shared production
# Atlas, polluting File.sourcePath with mac absolute paths). See start-dev.sh.
# OLA_ENV="dev"

# ------------------ Optional ------------------

# Gotenberg (PDF rendering) — only needed when exporting Quote/Invoice PDFs.
# Local dev: Vite占用 3000，docker 起 gotenberg 用 -p 3030:3000，所以下面写 :3030
# Production: Box3 跑 docker run ... -p 3000:3000，写 http://<Box3 Tailscale IP>:3000
# GOTENBERG_URL="http://localhost:3030"

# Resend (transactional email).
# RESEND_API="your_resend_api_key"

# Production only — CSV of allowed CORS origins (primary + legacy for overlap window).
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS="https://app.olatech.ai,https://app.olajob.cn"
